<title>USA: Knox County, Tenn., repriced, top yield raised.</title>
<headline>Knox County, Tenn., repriced, top yield raised.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-03-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Smith Barney Inc. said Wednesday that it repriced Knox County, Tenn., $27 million water and sewer revenue refunding improvement bonds, by raising the top yield to 5.774 from 5.75 percent.</p>
<p>The repricing follows:  </p>
<p>THE FIRST UTILITY DISTRICT OF</p>
<p>KNOX COUNTY, TENNESSEE</p>
<p>RE: $27,175,000*</p>
<p>WATER AND SEWER REVENUE REFUNDING AND</p>
<p>IMPROVEMENT BONDS</p>
<p>SERIES 1997 A</p>
<p>VERBAL AWARD.</p>
<p>PLEASE NOTE PRICE CHANGES 1997-2000, 2006 AND</p>
<p>2019.</p>
<p>    MOODY'S: Aaa		   S&amp;P: NAF</p>
<p>		 A3 UNDERLYING EXPECTED</p>
<p>MBIA INSURED</p>
<p>    DATED: 04/01/1997	    FIRST COUPON: 12/01/1997</p>
<p>DUE: 12/01</p>
